.TH buffer_mmapread_fd 3
.SH NAME
buffer_mmapread_fd \- map a file descriptor into a buffer using mmap
.SH SYNTAX
.B #include "buffer.h"

int buffer_mmapread_fd(buffer* \fIb\fP, fd_type \fIfd\fP);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B buffer_mmapread_fd
attempts to memory-map the file associated with the file descriptor
.I fd
directly into the buffer structure
.I b
using the
.I mmap_read_fd
function. 

If successful, the buffer's data pointer is pointed to the mapped memory,
and the deinitialization function is set to
.B buffer_munmap
to ensure the memory is unmapped when the buffer is destroyed.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 on success, or -1 if the memory mapping fails.
.SH SEE ALSO
mmap(2), buffer_munmap(3)